>> title: Masa para Pan Dulce
>> category: Pastry & Doughs
>> tags: dough, mexican, enriched, sweet, make-ahead
>> counters: Panadería
>> aka: masa para pan dulce, pan dulce dough, sweet bread dough, masa dulce, mexican sweet dough
>> pairs-with: conchas, cuernos, bigotes-de-pina
>> servings: 16
>> time: 3 hr 45 min
>> slack: forgiving — an enriched dough like this rises slowly and will take an extra half hour or a night in the fridge without complaint; the shaping is the part with a window, since a dough left to warm on the bench goes slack and the conchas lose their topping in the oven
>> step.1: stir, stand 10 min
>> step.2: beat in the eggs
>> step.3: add flour and salt, knead 10 min
>> step.4: work in the butter, rise until doubled
>> step.5: chill 1 hr, divide into 16

Stir @warm whole milk{3/4%cup}(180 mL; 110°F) with @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}(100 g) and @instant yeast{2 1/4%tsp}(7 g), then let it ~stand{10%min} until it foams. One dough stands under the conchas, the cuernos, the bigotes and the roles — the shop mixes it once and finishes it four ways.

Beat @eggs{3%large}(150 g) and @egg yolks{2}(36 g) into @&(~1)yeast mixture{}. The extra yolks are what make the crumb yellow and soft enough to pull apart rather than tear.

Add @bread flour{4%cup}(480 g) and @table salt{1 1/2%tsp}(9 g) to @&(~1)egg mixture{}, then ~knead{10%min} to a smooth, slack dough.

Work @softened unsalted butter{1/2%cup}(115 g) into @&(~1)dough{} a spoonful at a time until it is glossy, then let it ~rise{2%hr} until doubled.

Give @&(~1)risen dough{} a ~chill{1%hr} in the #refrigerator{}, then divide it into 16 pieces of about 65 g. Cold dough is what a shaped bun holds its shape from; warm dough spreads under the lid.
